# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reaper mapping for the Komplete Kontrol A-series (komplement)
#
# Usage (Komplete Kontrol A49, USB 17cc:1740):
#   komplement -m mappings/reaper.map -p 1740 -o /dev/uinput
#
# The default product ID in komplement is 1730 (A25); the A49 reports 1740,
# check your own with: lsusb | grep -i 17cc
#
# Every entry maps a button on the keyboard to one or more keystrokes which
# komplement sends through /dev/uinput. Reaper must have the keyboard focus,
# the keys below are the stock Reaper (Main section) shortcuts.
#
# Buttons are named as in doc/Supported_Keys.md. "Shift+X" entries are active
# while the SHIFT button (index 0) is held down.
#
# Two of the actions below have no stock Reaper shortcut and must be bound
# once in Reaper (Actions list, shortcut "?") - the key is given here, the
# action name is in the comment:
#   Metro : Ctrl+Shift+M   ->  Options: Toggle metronome
#   Solo  : Alt+Shift+S    ->  Track: Toggle solo for selected tracks
#
# Transport ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Space = play/stop (same toggle as the Reaper transport wheel); use Shift+Play
# for play/pause, Shift+Stop to jump to the project start.
Play=Space
Stop=Space
Record=LeftCtrl,R
Shift+Play=LeftCtrl,Space
Shift+Stop=W
Shift+Record=LeftCtrl,LeftAlt,B

# Editing --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Quantize = split items at the edit cursor, Ideas = insert a marker (markers
# are the closest thing to a scratch pad in Reaper), Shift+Ideas asks for the
# marker name so it can double as a note.
Undo=LeftCtrl,Z
Shift+Undo=LeftCtrl,LeftShift,Z
Quantize=S
Shift+Quantize=Q
Ideas=M
Shift+Ideas=LeftShift,M

# Grid and edit modes --------------------------------------------------------
# Scale = snapping, Arp = ripple editing, with SHIFT the grid display and
# auto-crossfading.
Scale=LeftAlt,S
Shift+Scale=LeftAlt,G
Arp=LeftAlt,P
Shift+Arp=LeftAlt,X

# Loop and metronome ---------------------------------------------------------
Loop=R
Shift+Loop=LeftCtrl,LeftAlt,L
Metro=LeftCtrl,LeftShift,M
Shift+Metro=LeftAlt,L

# Tempo and project ----------------------------------------------------------
Tempo=LeftShift,C
Shift+Tempo=LeftAlt,Enter

# Tracks ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Preset Up/Down walk the track list; with SHIFT they extend the track
# selection instead of replacing it.
#
# Page Left and Page Right (the two buttons beside the display) are deliberately
# *not* mapped: they belong to the screen daemon, which pages its display with
# them (doc/display-interface.md). Mapping them here as well would both page the
# screen and toggle mute in Reaper on one press. They used to be mapped as
# Mute/Solo, two names inherited from the original table that this keyboard has
# no use for - see doc/Captured_Codes.md.
Preset Up=LeftCtrl,LeftAlt,Up
Preset Down=LeftCtrl,LeftAlt,Down
Shift+Preset Up=LeftCtrl,LeftAlt,LeftShift,Up
Shift+Preset Down=LeftCtrl,LeftAlt,LeftShift,Down
Track=LeftCtrl,T

# Browser and plug-ins -------------------------------------------------------
# Browser = media explorer (audition loops), Plug-In = FX chain of the
# selected item/take, with SHIFT the FX browser and the external editor.
Browser=LeftCtrl,LeftAlt,X
Shift+Browser=LeftShift,F
Plug-In=LeftShift,E
Shift+Plug-In=LeftCtrl,LeftAlt,E

# Zoom -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Octave Down/Up zoom the arrangement horizontally, with SHIFT they change the
# track height.
Octave Down=Minus
Octave Up=Equal
Shift+Octave Down=PageDown
Shift+Octave Up=PageUp

# Jog ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Turning the 4D dial moves the edit cursor, and while playing the play
# position follows it. One click steps by grid division (Ctrl+Shift+Left/Right
# = "Move cursor left/right to grid division"), holding SHIFT steps by a small
# amount instead (plain Left/Right = "Move cursor left/right").
#
# If "fast" and "fine" feel swapped, the other way round is Ctrl+Left /
# Ctrl+Right ("Rewind a little bit" / "Fast forward a little bit"), which seek
# the play position directly.
4D CCW=LeftCtrl,LeftShift,Left
4D CW=LeftCtrl,LeftShift,Right
Shift+4D CCW=Left
Shift+4D CW=Right

# 4D dial and the rotary touch sensors ----------------------------------------
# The bit values behind these names were measured on an A49, see
# doc/Captured_Codes.md. Up/Down walk the track list, Left/Right nudge the time
# selection, 4D Button toggles the selected track's volume envelope, and the
# 4D dial jogs the edit/play cursor - all stock Reaper shortcuts.
#
# (Until the payload's fifth byte was decoded these could not fire at all: the
# scan loop stopped at button 20.)
4D Up=LeftCtrl,LeftAlt,Up
4D Down=LeftCtrl,LeftAlt,Down
4D Left=Comma
4D Right=Dot
4D Button=V

# Knobs ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing here: the rotary touch sensors are deliberately left unmapped.
#
# The A49's knobs are capacitive, so a touch sensor fires on *every* turn, not
# only when a knob is deliberately touched. Mapped, it sent a keystroke of its own
# on top of the rotation: Reaper selected another track at the same moment the
# knob was setting the volume of the one that was current, and in Reaper's Learn
# dialog the keystroke was what got caught instead of the CC.
#
# Turning a knob is not routed through komplement at all: the knobs send MIDI CC
# 14..21 or 22..29 (channel 1, one CC per knob, absolute values, one step per
# detent) depending on the keyboard's own MIDI template - check which with
# `aseqdump -p <the keyboard's port>`, see doc/Captured_Codes.md. Enable the
# keyboard's own MIDI port as a control input in Reaper, then learn that CC to
# "Track: Set volume for selected tracks (MIDI CC/OSC only)" and the knob drives
# whatever track is *current*, or to "Track: Set volume for track 01..08 (MIDI
# CC/OSC only)" for a fixed track each. Learning both numbers is the safe way
# round a template change: Reaper keeps several MIDI bindings per action. The values
# are the knob's own position, so a track's volume jumps to it on the first turn;
# a knob that cannot jump would need this tool to read the CCs and send MCU volume
# for the current track instead, which is not written yet.
#
# Selecting tracks lives on Preset Up/Down (Ctrl+Alt+Up/Down) and on the tracks
# page of the display (doc/display-interface.md).

# Button34..Button39 were silent on the A49 (nothing in the payload either).
